higher English requirements\nProgrammes with external English requirements\nDates and deadlines\nHow to apply\nPrepare your documents\nApply as a New Zealand secondary school student\nP\u016baha\u2014log in or sign up\nYour Offer\nEnrol for courses\nChoosing your courses\nCredit transfer and exemptions\nFind an agent\nApplication and enrolment terms and conditions\nPrepare to study\nYour offer\nEnrol for courses\nDates and deadlines\nStudent visa\nAccommodation\nAccommodation for Scholarship students\nInsurance\nStudentsafe University insurance\nInternational buddy programme\nCheck your health needs\nCourse planning\nPreparing for travel\nArrival meeting service\nInternational Orientation\nOrientation and start dates\nTimetable\nCurrent international students\nInternational orientation\nStudentsafe Inbound University insurance\nVisa support\nStudy support\nContact International Student Experience\nHealth and safety\nRe-enrolling\nManaaki New Zealand Scholarships programme support\nDates and deadlines\nApply to study at Victoria University of Wellington by these deadlines. This will ensure you have time to apply for a student visa and accommodation.\nApplication deadlines\nYou can apply to study at Victoria University of Wellington at any time. You should apply as early as possible to make sure you have time to apply for a student visa and accommodation before you travel to New Zealand.\nTrimester 1 (February)\u2014application deadline 8 December\nTrimester 2 (July)\u2014application deadline 1 May\nTrimester 3 (November)\u2014application deadline 1 September.\nApplications received after these dates will be assessed on a case-by-case basis.\nPostgraduate early application deadlines\nThe following postgraduate programmes have early application deadlines due to their selection process. To be considered for entry into these programmes, you must apply by the dates listed under each programme heading. Please check all the conditions.\nGraduate Diploma of Teaching (Early Childhood Education, Primary, or Secondary)\nApply by 1 November.\nThere is an early start date for this programme.\nMaster of Arts in Creative Writing\nApply by 1 November.\nApplications are processed after this date and not on a rolling basis.\nThe outcomes will be available around November and December each year.\nMaster of Conservation Biology\nApply by 1 October for a Trimester 1 start.\nThere is an early start date for this programme.\nMaster of Marine Conservation\nApply by 1 October for a Trimester 1 start.\nApply by 1 March for a Trimester 2 start.\nThere are early start dates for this programme.\nMaster of Nursing Practice\nApply by 1 November.\nThere is an early start date for this programme.\nMaster of Science in Cognitive and Behavioural Neuroscience / Forensic Psychology / Cross-cultural Psychology / Bachelor of Science with Honours (Psychology)\nApply by 1 November.\nApplications are processed after this date and not on a rolling basis.\nThe outcomes will be available around November and December each year.\nMaster of Teaching and Learning (Primary or Secondary)\nApply by 1 November.\nThere is an early start date for this programme.\nThe selection interview for the Master of Teaching and Learning (Secondary) will only be held in Wellington and you will be expected to attend in person.\nThe selection interview for the Master of Teaching and Learning (Primary) can be conducted online.\nAccommodation deadlines\nYou should apply for your student accommodation as early as possible. This will give you the best chance of getting a place in your preferred hall.\nThe University offers many accommodation options for international students. Hall applications open on the following dates for each trimester:\nTrimester 1\u20141 August (the year before you begin your studies)\nTrimester 2\u20141 April\nTrimester 3\u20141 August.\nWe recommend getting your application in as soon as possible to avoid disappointment.\nMake sure you apply in time to organise your student visa and travel to New Zealand. Find out when you need to arrive\u2014check your Orientation and class start dates.\nConnect with us\nContact us\nFind an agent\nInformation sessions\nGet a student guide\nEmergencies\nFaculties\nArchitecture and Design Innovation\nBusiness and Government\nEducation, Health, and Psychological Sciences\nGraduate Research\nHumanities and Social Sciences\nLaw\nScience and Engineering\nContacts and directories\nStaff directory\nMedia enquiries\nFind a researcher\nHealth and safety\nCampuses\nKelburn Campus\nPipitea Campus\nTe Aro Campus\nAuckland Premises\nStudy\nProgrammes and courses\nApply and enrol\nScholarships\nAccommodation\nSchools hub\nStudents\nLibrary\nServices and support\nFinancial survival\nKey dates\nCourses\nP\u016baha\u2014Student portal\nNuku\u2014Learning environment\nLibrary\nStaff\nStaff email\nStaff Service Centre\nMyTools for staff\nTeaching support\nWorking here\nCurrent vacancies\nAlumni\nStay connected\nGiving\nDonate\nLatest news\nEvents\nResearch expertise\nPublications\nSocial media\n0800 04 04 04\n+64 4 472 1000\ninfo@vuw.ac.nz\nEmergency: 0800 842 8888\nSite info\nSite map\nFeedback\nGlossary\nPrivacy\nCopyright \u00a9 Victoria University of Wellington, New Zealand", "links": [["", "javascript:;"], ["", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/international/applying/dates-and-deadlines/_edit"], ["", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/"], ["Te Kahupapa ki Tai International", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/international"], ["P\u016baha", "https://puaha.wgtn.ac.nz/"], ["Nuku", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/teaching-support/teaching-with-technology/log-in-to-nuku"], ["Staff", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/staff"], ["Apply to study", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/study/apply-enrol"], ["Apply", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/study/apply-enrol"], ["", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/"], ["Te Kahupapa Future students", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/study"], ["Te Kahupapa ki Tai International students", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/international"], ["Ng\u0101 \u0101konga Current students", "ht